Aug 19 19:59:45 silt-ft-val-d-2323b09-20931 silt[1017]: bond: objective re-challenge TTL defaulted to 32 blocks for this untrusted (objective) swarm — standing lapses this many blocks after a validator's latest bond proof unless it renews, so a released plot can't keep voting. Override with -bond-ttl (0 disables; safe only for a trusted/demo swarm).
Aug 19 19:59:45 silt-ft-val-d-2323b09-20931 silt[1017]: consensus: Byzantine quorum sizing defaulted ON for this untrusted (objective) swarm — a commit needs a supermajority of the qualified bonded set so two quorums always share an honest validator. Override with -byzantine-quorum=false (safe only for a trusted swarm).
Aug 19 19:59:45 silt-ft-val-d-2323b09-20931 silt[1017]: consensus: operator-margin defaulted to 2 for this untrusted (objective) swarm — the C2 maturity shed discounts the bond-distinct Nakamoto coefficient by M, so one operator splitting real stake across ~M NodeIDs cannot fake the decentralization that sheds the launch anchors. Override with -operator-margin (1 = no split margin; safe only for a trusted/single-operator swarm).
Aug 19 19:59:45 silt-ft-val-d-2323b09-20931 silt[1017]: consensus: epoch-blocks defaulted to 8 for this untrusted (objective) swarm — after the young→mature handoff the finality quorum and validator set are frozen per epoch (rotated at finalized boundary blocks), so churning bonds cannot let two conflicting commits finalize against two different sets. Override with -epoch-blocks, identically across the swarm (0 disables; safe only for a trusted/demo swarm).
